<title>ITALY: Italy's EU payments gap narrows in 1995.</title>
<headline>Italy's EU payments gap narrows in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury said on Thursday that Italy paid more to the European Union than it received in 1995 but the gap had narrowed.</p>
<p>A Treasury statement said Italy's payments into the EU's budget totalled 15.8 trillion lire in 1995, compared to transfers from the EU of 14.7 trillion.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been a noticeable reduction in the negative gap, because of the entrance of new member states and because of the concentration in 1995 of community credits allocated at the end of 1994,&quot; the statement said. -- Rome newsroom +396 678 2505</p>
</text>
